
Implement Phase 5: Rich Markdown Support for the KB Admin Knowledge Assistant.

IMPORTANT

- Do NOT rewrite the existing architecture.
- Do NOT replace the current chat system.
- Extend the existing Knowledge Assistant rendering pipeline only.
- Reuse the existing APIs, retrieval pipeline, LangSmith integration and KB articles.
- Backward compatibility is mandatory.

====================================================
OBJECTIVE
====================================================

Upgrade the KB Admin chatbot so documentation is rendered as rich interactive content instead of plain text.

The assistant should support professional technical documentation similar to GitHub, Notion and Microsoft Learn.

====================================================
FEATURES TO IMPLEMENT
====================================================

1. Rich Markdown Rendering

Support full Markdown including:

- headings
- bold
- italic
- underline (if existing renderer supports it)
- block quotes
- ordered lists
- unordered lists
- nested lists
- checklists
- horizontal rules
- hyperlinks
- inline code
- fenced code blocks
- tables

Ensure formatting is preserved from KB articles.

----------------------------------------------------

2. Syntax Highlighting

Support syntax highlighting for:

- TypeScript
- JavaScript
- Python
- JSON
- YAML
- SQL
- Bash
- HTML
- CSS

Provide copy-to-clipboard for every code block.

----------------------------------------------------

3. Images

Render images embedded in markdown.

Support:

- local KB assets
- hosted images
- responsive sizing
- captions
- click to enlarge
- lazy loading
- loading placeholders

Gracefully handle broken images.

----------------------------------------------------

4. Diagrams

Render Mermaid diagrams directly inside chat.

Support:

- Flowcharts
- Sequence diagrams
- Class diagrams
- State diagrams
- Entity Relationship diagrams
- Journey diagrams
- Gantt charts
- Pie charts

If diagram rendering fails,
show the original markdown instead of breaking the page.

----------------------------------------------------

5. Graphics

Support rendering for:

SVG

PNG

JPEG

GIF

WebP

Maintain responsive scaling.

----------------------------------------------------

6. Documentation Experience

Improve article readability.

Implement:

Table of contents

Section anchors

Collapsible sections

Expandable code examples

Copy buttons

Sticky headings where appropriate

Smooth scrolling

Readable spacing

Dark mode compatibility

----------------------------------------------------

7. Technical Callouts

Support styled blocks such as:

Info

Warning

Success

Error

Tip

Important

Notes

If KB articles already use markdown callouts,
render them correctly.

----------------------------------------------------

8. Mathematical Expressions

If markdown contains LaTeX,

support:

Inline math

Block math

without affecting existing rendering.

----------------------------------------------------

9. Embedded Media

Support embedded:

YouTube links

Documentation links

GitHub links

PDF links

Open safely in a new tab.

----------------------------------------------------

10. Performance

Do not negatively impact chatbot performance.

Implement:

lazy rendering

memoization where appropriate

virtualization if large documents

avoid unnecessary rerenders

----------------------------------------------------

11. Security

Sanitize all HTML.

Prevent XSS.

Disallow unsafe scripts.

Validate external links.

